<p class="eyebrow">Svelte pattern</p>

# useMediaQuery

<CopyMarkdownButton url="/docs/hooks/use-media-query.md" />

The upstream React page documents a `useMediaQuery` hook with Tailwind-like shorthand. COSS for Svelte
does not export a `useMediaQuery` hook. Svelte 5 already provides the reactive `MediaQuery` class in
`svelte/reactivity`, so this port documents that native API instead of inventing a package export.

## Usage

### Breakpoints

Pass a complete CSS media query and provide `false` as the server fallback. Read `.current` in markup,
`$derived`, or `$effect`.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { MediaQuery } from "svelte/reactivity";

  const isDesktop = new MediaQuery("(min-width: 1024px)", false);
  const isMobile = new MediaQuery("(max-width: 799px)", false);
  const isTablet = new MediaQuery("(min-width: 800px) and (max-width: 1023px)", false);
</script>

{#if isDesktop.current}
  <DesktopNav />
{:else}
  <MobileNav />
{/if}
```

Use CSS container or media queries when only layout changes. Conditional rendering is appropriate
when the component tree or behavior must differ.

### Pointer and preference queries

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { MediaQuery } from "svelte/reactivity";

  const isTouch = new MediaQuery("(pointer: coarse)", false);
  const prefersDark = new MediaQuery("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)", false);
  const prefersReducedMotion = new MediaQuery("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)", false);
</script>
```

## Breakpoints

The upstream COSS hook used these values. Keep the queries in sync with the breakpoints in your
Tailwind theme.

| Name  | Value  |
| ----- | ------ |
| `sm`  | 640px  |
| `md`  | 800px  |
| `lg`  | 1024px |
| `xl`  | 1280px |
| `2xl` | 1536px |
| `3xl` | 1600px |
| `4xl` | 2000px |

## SSR behavior

The second constructor argument is the value used on the server. `false` matches the upstream hook's
server behavior and prevents the server from guessing a viewport. A branch may change after hydration
when the browser query is true, so prefer CSS when both branches contain important content.

## Examples

Resize the viewport to see the values update.

<MediaQueryDemo />

## API

```ts
import { MediaQuery } from "svelte/reactivity";

const query = new MediaQuery("(min-width: 800px)", false);
query.current; // boolean
```
